T1 -- bond restoring force & stiffness (unison pair, symmetric branch)
==============================================================================
[a] kernel identity G'(psi) = -0.5*p*(G/h)*sin(psi): VERIFIED (diff == 0)
[b] on-branch kernel dVdd = (p*S/(2C)) * h^(2p-1) * sin(S*delta/(2C)),  h = (1+cos(S*delta/(2C)))/2 : VERIFIED
[c] kernel fixed-phase dVdd|branch == d/d(delta)[1 - G(psi)^2] (total on-branch derivative): EXACTLY EQUAL
    (equal unison pair only: moving d at fixed phases changes psi_f and psi_b by the
     same -S/(2C)*dd, i.e. fixed-phase motion tracks the symmetric branch.)
[d] linearisation: dVdd|branch = S**2*p/(4*C**2) * delta + O(delta^3)
    ==> K_b = -d(dd/dt)/d(delta)|0 = kappa * (kd*geo*gpl*res) * Sm * p*S^2/(4*C^2)
    COEFFICIENT CHECK vs the guess p*S^2/(2*C^2): derived/guess = 1/2
    >>> SURPRISE: the guessed stiffness coefficient is 2x TOO LARGE; exact is p*S^2/(4*C^2). <<<
[e] sign: dd/dt = -kappa*kd*geo(d)*Sm*(p*S/(2C))*h^(2p-1)*sin(S*delta/(2C));
    for |delta| < 2*pi*C/S = dstar the sin carries sign(delta), h^(2p-1) > 0, geo >= 0,
    so sign(dd/dt) = -sign(delta): two-sided restoring over the whole rung basin,
    PROVIDED geo > 0, i.e. d < ri+rj = contact (lens open). Beyond contact the force is exactly 0.

