conclusion: vacuum is EXACTLY inert (Sm=0).  Crumb pairs have max bond velocity 0.21x (eps=1e-3)
to 0.66x (eps=1e-2) of the 0.17 repulsion scale, BUT their rung sits at 36% overlap where
repulsion exceeds the bond maximum by an order of magnitude; and once pushed out to ~10%
overlap the gate factor has collapsed (ratio ~1e-4 to 1e-3).  Crumbs cannot bind; no vacuum
crystallisation from the P15 term.

==============================================================================
T5 -- mu-convexity re-check (geopress criterion), sympy
==============================================================================
[per-cell] mu_i = dU/dE_i at fixed partner:  mu_i = k*delta^(alpha-1)*r_i/(3*E_i)
  d(mu_i)/dE_i = (k*r_i/(9*E_i^2)) * delta^(alpha-2) * [ (alpha-1)*r_i - 2*delta ]  -- check: VERIFIED (exact symbolic at alpha=2,3,4; numeric residual < 4.4e-16 at 6 random general-alpha points)
  => mu falls with E_i  iff  delta/r_i > (alpha-1)/2     [claim CONFIRMED]
  alpha = 2:  delta/r > 1/2  -- confirmed.
  (alpha=2 explicit d(mu)/dE_i: k*r_0*(-E_i**(1/3)*r_0 - 2*E_j**(1/3)*r_0 + 2*d*e_0**(1/3))/(9*E_i**(5/3)*e_0**(2/3)) )

[symmetric-growth caveat] if BOTH cells grow with one E (delta = 2*r(E) - d):
  d^2U/dE^2 = (4k*r^2/(9E^2)) * delta^(alpha-2) * [ (alpha-1) - delta/r ]  -- symbolic check: VERIFIED
  => along that path the criterion is delta/r > (alpha-1)  (alpha=2 -> delta/r > 1): 2x harsher.
  The stated geopress criterion is the PER-CELL chemical potential (partner fixed) -- that one
  is exactly delta/r > (alpha-1)/2.  Constants k, r_0, e_0 drop out in both (scale-free).

numeric finite-difference confirmation (k=1, r0=e0=1, E=1 so r=1):
  per-cell, alpha=2, delta/r = 0.4:  d(mu)/dE = +2.222198e-02  (rises)
  per-cell, alpha=2, delta/r = 0.6:  d(mu)/dE = -2.222264e-02  (falls)
  symmetric, alpha=2, delta/r = 0.9:  d(mu)/dE = +4.444403e-02  (rises)
  symmetric, alpha=2, delta/r = 1.1:  d(mu)/dE = -4.444528e-02  (falls)

