  cube                     V= 8 E=12  rank(R)=12  floppy=3V-6-rank= 6   [sv gap: kept>=1.414e+00, dropped<=0.000e+00]   FLOPPY
  icosahedron              V=12 E=30  rank(R)=30  floppy=3V-6-rank= 0   [sv gap: kept>=7.654e-01, dropped<=0.000e+00]   SHEAR-RIGID (isostatic)
  ring6 + 3 long diagonals V= 6 E= 9  rank(R)= 8  floppy=3V-6-rank= 4   [sv gap: kept>=1.225e+00, dropped<=1.406e-16]   FLOPPY

shear-rigid seeds: octahedron (floppy 0) and icosahedron (floppy 0) -- both isostatic
(E = 3V-6 exactly).  ring6 has 6 floppy modes, cube has 6 (shear/flex), ring6+3diag has 4.
note: ring6+3diag has rank E-1 = 8, i.e. one SELF-STRESS (ring tension balanced by diagonal
compression through the centre), so adding 3 members removes only 2 floppy modes (6 -> 4),
not 3: in-plane bracing of a symmetric ring wastes a member on the self-stress.

==============================================================================
SURPRISES / deviations from the task's stated expectations
==============================================================================
1. K_b coefficient is p*S^2/(4*C^2), NOT p*S^2/(2*C^2): the guessed stiffness is 2x too large.
   K_b(x=0.325) = 10.9977802012467 * kappa per t.u.
2. The outward capture edge is NOT gate-set: the lens area (and the whole bond force) vanishes
   exactly at d = contact = 2r.  Bond and repulsion share the same support (overlap only).
   Full-geometry capture: force max at delta = 0.0607582801115332 (+ side) / -0.222946344078248 (- side); 10% points 0.127601059021973 / -0.514537195613401.  Strongly asymmetric.
3. T3: NO entrainment is needed to lock -- psi_f + psi_b = -S*d/C is a phase-independent
   identity, so the first-order restoring force is split-independent.  Pure phase advance
   converges to the same d_inf as entrained runs; entrainment only re-opens the frozen gate
   offset.  The specified ONE-SIDED entrainment lands on the psi_f=0 branch, not the
   symmetric branch (needs two-sided pulls); dynamically irrelevant at first order.
4. T4: the fl0 floor makes crumb bonding scale as sqrt(eps*fl0) (weaker than any load but
   BOOSTED above linear-in-eps); still, a crumb pair's rung lies at 36% overlap where
   repulsion exceeds the bond max 5.5x (eps=1e-2) to 17x (eps=1e-3) one-sided (11-35x
   relative), so crumbs cannot bind.  Vacuum exactly inert.
5. T5: criterion delta/r > (alpha-1)/2 CONFIRMED for the per-cell mu (partner fixed);
   along the symmetric both-cells-grow path it is delta/r > (alpha-1) (factor 2 harsher) --
   which derivative geopress measures matters.
6. T6: ring6 floppy=6, cube floppy=6; octahedron and icosahedron floppy=0 (only shear-rigid seeds).
